      "type": "markdown",
      "markdown": "Holm argues that seemingly incompatible algorithmic fairness criteria are applications of one account of fairness, and differ over what grounds people’s claims to an allocated good. <citation id=\"u-D6AG238X\" loc=\"s2.4-s2.5\"/>\n\n> “All four performance parity criteria can be understood as applications of a single principle of fairness defended by John Broome (1990) according to which fairness in the distribution of a good between people consists in the proportional satisfaction of their claims to the good.” — p. 266. <citation id=\"u-D6AG238X\" loc=\"s2.4\"/>"
    }
  ],
